Use a project settings file while its content stays the same

Records that you trust the settings file at PATH with its current content.
snouty then uses the file. When the content changes, snouty stops with an error
until you trust the file again. Read the file before you trust it: it can set
where snouty sends your credentials.

snouty keeps the record in trust.toml, in the global settings directory.

Examples:
  snouty settings trust
  snouty settings trust path/to/.snouty.toml

Usage: snouty settings trust [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          The project settings file
          
          [default: .snouty.toml]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
